    "6ak4ZScH_gc:Q01": {
      "video_id": "6ak4ZScH_gc",
      "start": 10.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "why the pelvis fires forward and why even though the pelvis fires forward, I am telling you to imagine a feeling of yanking your pelvis back"
    },
    "6ak4ZScH_gc:Q03": {
      "video_id": "6ak4ZScH_gc",
      "start": 40.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "The main crux of the question here is when, if at all, does the pelvis physically rotate forwards? What does that feel like? And what should you try to do?"
    },
    "6ak4ZScH_gc:Q04": {
      "video_id": "6ak4ZScH_gc",
      "start": 50.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "clarify exactly why, even though your pelvis is going to physically rotate forward, I think you should intend to take this side and fire it backwards."
    },
    "6ak4ZScH_gc:Q07": {
      "video_id": "6ak4ZScH_gc",
      "start": 156.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "And so, that's the key is the same tension that flings your shoulder forward, flings your hip backwards. That's the same thing."
    },
    "6ak4ZScH_gc:Q08": {
      "video_id": "6ak4ZScH_gc",
      "start": 173.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "And what it is is it's stretched when the shoulders and the hips are trying to be twisted opposite."
    },
    "6ak4ZScH_gc:Q09": {
      "video_id": "6ak4ZScH_gc",
      "start": 198.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "Well, what's the best way now if this bit if pretend this back anchor is the shoulders. What is the best way to get this boom, through? It's to go boom, like that."
    },
    "6ak4ZScH_gc:Q10": {
      "video_id": "6ak4ZScH_gc",
      "start": 209.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "Boom, and pull boom on that front anchor just a little bit more before I let it fling forwards."
    },
    "6ak4ZScH_gc:Q13": {
      "video_id": "6ak4ZScH_gc",
      "start": 296.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "I'm not going to tension it because if my shoulder stretch against it, now I can't move it forwards nearly as much and I can feel myself pulling it back."
    },
    "6ak4ZScH_gc:Q19": {
      "video_id": "6ak4ZScH_gc",
      "start": 463.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "So you want to feel your pelvis under tension getting pulled backwards as you accelerate your shoulder, but it's not going to move backwards on most shots"
    },
    "6ak4ZScH_gc:Q20": {
      "video_id": "6ak4ZScH_gc",
      "start": 476.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "it is going to be moving forwards, yanked backwards, and then it's just going to slow down. It's not actually going to reverse direction on many shots."
    },
    "KU7FHy1qQOI:Q01": {
      "video_id": "KU7FHy1qQOI",
      "start": 18.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "hitting the ball in the center of the string bed. So you know, as you coordinate your kinetic chain better and better, you might get 10 20 30 40% more power."
    },
    "KU7FHy1qQOI:Q02": {
      "video_id": "KU7FHy1qQOI",
      "start": 87.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "You could do everything right. You get this to fire. You get this to fire. Your chest fires you. Everything comes through... And then if you hit here instead of here, you've just undone everything"
    },
    "KU7FHy1qQOI:Q04": {
      "video_id": "KU7FHy1qQOI",
      "start": 137.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "The most important parts of your body for hitting hard are your eyes and your feet. And then in order to use them effectively, you need to know where your swing ends up in space."
    },
    "KU7FHy1qQOI:Q08": {
      "video_id": "KU7FHy1qQOI",
      "start": 336.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "without intent, it doesn't happen. So, a lot of times I see this where it's like all I really kind of did there was vaguely watch the ball and then just kind of vaguely try to hit it"
    },
    "KU7FHy1qQOI:Q10": {
      "video_id": "KU7FHy1qQOI",
      "start": 415.0,
      "about": "demonstrator_induced",
      "text": "Now, do a couple where your feet get stuck where you're not really paying attention. You don't really split step and all of a sudden a slow ball like this, you can't hit it hard."
    },
    "KU7FHy1qQOI:Q17": {
      "video_id": "KU7FHy1qQOI",
      "start": 780.0,
      "about": "general",
      "text": "what I see from a lot of players that I work with as they come up for shorter balls is they they see a shorter ball, but they don't actually turn sideways."
    }
  },
